<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Felix Dzerzhinsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1877–1926</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Felix Dzerzhinsky was a Polish-born Bolshevik revolutionary who founded and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheka">Cheka</a>, the Soviet secret police, from December 1917. Under his direction it carried out the Red Terror against opponents during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>. He later also headed the Supreme Council of the National Economy, and his statue outside the secret police headquarters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> was pulled down in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/felix-dzerzhinsky.jpg" alt="Felix Dzerzhinsky" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.S. Nappelbaum · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Feliks_Dzier%C5%BCy%C5%84ski.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
